==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|sól|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|sōwul|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|sóh₂wl̥|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with Old Church Slavonic {{term|sc=Cyrl|слъньцє|tr=slŭnĭce|lang=cu}}, Latin {{term|sol|sōl|lang=la}}, Ancient Greek {{term|ἥλιος|sc=polytonic|tr=hēlios|lang=grc}}, Sanskrit {{term|sc=Deva|सूर|tr=sūra|lang=sa}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/souːl/|lang=is}} ({{audio|Sól.ogg|listen}})
*: {{rhymes|ouːl|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|sólar|sólir}}

# the [[sun]] {{gloss|star around which the Earth revolves}}
#* ''Á Sprengisandi'' (“On Sprengisandur”) by [[w:en:Grímur Thomsen|Grímur Thomsen]]
#*: Ríðum, ríðum og rekum yfir sandinn,
#*: rennur '''sól''' á bak við Arnarfell,
#*: hér á reiki er margur óhreinn andinn,
#*: úr því fer að skyggja á jökulsvell;
#*: Drottinn leiði drösulinn minn,
#*: drjúgur verður síðasti áfanginn.
#*:: Ride, ride, ride hard across the sands,
#*:: the '''sun''' is settling behind Arnarfell.
#*:: Here many spirits of the dark
#*:: threaten in the gloom over the glacier's ice.
#*:: The Lord leads my horse,
#*:: it is still a long, long way home.
#: '''''Sólin''' er [[björt]].''
#:: The '''sun''' is [[bright]].
# [[sun]] {{gloss|applied to any star or used metaphorically}}

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-f-s2|s|ó|l}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|the sun}} {{l|is|sunna}} (''poetic'')

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|sólber}}
* {{l|is|sólarljós}}
* {{l|is|sólmyrkvi}}
* {{l|is|forsæla}}

